<PageHero eyebrow="Resource" title="How Long Do You Need to Live in Spain Before Spanish Nationality?" description="There is a general residence period and reduced periods for specific groups. The applicant’s nationality and circumstances determine which period is relevant." primaryLabel="Contact the firm" primaryHref="/en/contact" secondaryLabel="More resources" secondaryHref="/en/resources" note="General information · Check the current official source before acting" />
<section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>There is a general period and reduced periods</h2><p>The residence period is not the same for every applicant. The general rules include:</p><ul><li><strong>10 years</strong> as the general period.</li><li><strong>5 years</strong> for people who have obtained refugee status.</li><li><strong>2 years</strong> for nationals by origin of Ibero-American countries, Andorra, the Philippines, Equatorial Guinea or Portugal, and for Sephardic applicants under the legal framework.</li><li><strong>1 year</strong> in specific cases provided by law, including certain applicants born in Spain or married to a Spanish citizen.</li></ul><h2>Check your nationality and residence history</h2><p>The relevant period must be checked together with the legal character and continuity of residence and the other requirements of the application.</p><p><a href="https://www.mjusticia.gob.es/en/ciudadania/nacionalidad/que-es-nacionalidad/como-adquiere-nacionalidad/modos-adquisicion" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check the Ministry of Justice information →</a> <a href="https://www.boe.es/buscar/act.php?id=BOE-A-1889-4763" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check Article 22 of the Civil Code at the BOE →</a></p></div></section>
